nixpkgs: nixos-26.05 (see flake.lock; unchanged from 0/3/1)
changes: First version of series 0.4 — the bnox-bg/agenthub lessons (D-018, D-019, D-020). BREAKING vs 0.3 (minor bump): the broker requires logins, outbound and inbound are locked by default, outboundHTTPS is gone. (1) NATS identity (D-018, modules/nats): no anonymous access; an nkey per identity generated on the host at runtime (bnox-nats-keygen, from bnox-bg's validated nkey.py) — never in git or the store — which also fills the implied nats_seed slot; permissions computed at eval: a NATS thing gets things.<name>.> + its own stream (things-<name>, the G5 durable pull-consumer JS surface), plus host grants on other things (bnox.things.<n>.nats.grants.<dep> = <role>|"offer"), where the dep's .bnox `nats = { offer; roles; }` caps them — roles must fit inside the offer, grants need the dep in deps, all checked at eval; nats.extra = visible host escape hatch. bnox service identities: ops (full, root-only seed), bnox-webhook-receiver (host.deploy.*.changed), bnox-deploy-dispatcher (sub host.deploy.>), bnox-deploy-<thing> (sync+build, host.deploy.<thing>.>); host extras via bnox.nats.identities. Runtime config assembled by bnox-nats-auth (relative includes — G12; validated with nats-server -t — G9; broker restarted only on change), one JetStream stream per NATS thing (bnox-nats-streams, complete config — G8). The deploy dispatcher is now Go (nats-py could not do nkey auth — G4; from bnox-bg's deploy-bridge). Fixes 0.3's anonymous pipeline publishes (G23). (2) env (D-019): thing-level plain config, .bnox defaults, host wins per key, both runtimes. (3) egress locked by default (D-019): .bnox `egress` (domains | "any") ∩ host `egress.grant`; a domain list gets a per-thing tinyproxy (127.0.0.1, ports from bnox.egress.basePort, anchored ERE filter, default deny) + proxy env, containers via slirp 10.0.2.2; any/any = direct; nothing = loopback only (host-install units no longer allow any). hardening.network.outboundHTTPS removed (assertion). (4) inbound locked by default (D-019): host components.<c>.inbound (internal|tailnet|public, default internal) ∩ .bnox exposure cap; one vhost generator for all shapes and both runtimes (host-install dashboards included); tailnet = Caddy remote_ip guard (100.64.0.0/10, fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48). (5) host-install switches (D-020): .bnox shell = true (bash instead of nologin, G33), nixLd = true (nix-ld + NIX_LD vars in units, G26). (6) bnox.lib.mkImage (D-020): fakeNss passwd/group, HOME=/root, CA store + SSL_CERT_FILE, /tmp (G18/G19/G30). (7) bnox-validate (D-020): generated from the computed permission matrix, every identity × every probe subject, plus anonymous rejection. Verification so far: eval of a test host covering both runtimes, grants/roles/offer errors, egress modes, inbound levels; tinyproxy filter and Caddy tailnet guard checked locally; dispatcher compiles; bnox-validate passes shellcheck. NOT yet deployed — the done rule (D-017 §6) applies.
